NOTE BEFORE COMMITTING — replace this file with the full legal code.

GitHub: Add file -> Create new file -> type "LICENSE" -> "Choose a license
template" -> Creative Commons Attribution 4.0. That inserts the complete,
verbatim legal text and makes GitHub's license detection show the CC BY 4.0
badge in the sidebar. A summary-only LICENSE is legally weaker than the full
text and will not be detected.

Also replace <ATTRIBUTION NAME> above with the name you want credited. Under
CC BY this is functional, not cosmetic — it is the name downstream users are
required to attribute.
